  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "08836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 0,
      "content": "CSUF General Transfer Information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5f836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. See the Admissions website for transfer admission requirements &amp; Admissions deadlines See approved General Education courses at CSU Fullerton. See Associate Degree for Transfer. See the Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP) .",
      "contentHtml": "<blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">University Catalog</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the Admissions website for </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/prospectivestudent/transferlocaladmissionarea.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">transfer admission requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> &amp; </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/deadlines/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Admissions deadlines</a></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.fullerton.edu/undergraduate/general-education/approved-courses.html#box5\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">approved General Education </a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">courses at CSU Fullerton. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/associate-degree-for-transfer-major-and-campus-search.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Associate Degree for Transfer.</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/external-exams/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP)</a><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/attend/student-services/casper/Pages/external-exam-credit.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">.</a></blockquote>"
    },
    {
      "id": "12836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About This Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0e836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The Bachelor of Arts in English ( Link ) prepares students to enter professions that expect excellence in reading and writing, including education, publishing, creative and professional writing, public service, law, medicine or business. The major may be combined with preparation for elementary and secondary school teaching. In addition, it can provide a foundation for students who intend to pursue advanced degrees in preparation for teaching at the college level. The curriculum is designed to prepare students to examine the diverse ways in which writing and literature let us see the past, understand advanced rhetorical and linguistic techniques, and make sense of the world through narrative.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>The&nbsp;Bachelor&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;in&nbsp;English&nbsp;(<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=101&amp;poid=47332&amp;returnto=15150\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>)&nbsp;prepares&nbsp;students&nbsp;to&nbsp;enter&nbsp;professions&nbsp;that&nbsp;expect&nbsp;excellence&nbsp;in&nbsp;reading&nbsp;and&nbsp;writing,&nbsp;including&nbsp;education,&nbsp;publishing,&nbsp;creative&nbsp;and&nbsp;professional&nbsp;writing,&nbsp;public&nbsp;service,&nbsp;law,&nbsp;medicine&nbsp;or&nbsp;business.&nbsp;The&nbsp;major&nbsp;may&nbsp;be&nbsp;combined&nbsp;with&nbsp;preparation&nbsp;for&nbsp;elementary&nbsp;and&nbsp;secondary&nbsp;school&nbsp;teaching.&nbsp;In&nbsp;addition,&nbsp;it&nbsp;can&nbsp;provide&nbsp;a&nbsp;foundation&nbsp;for&nbsp;students&nbsp;who&nbsp;intend&nbsp;to&nbsp;pursue&nbsp;advanced&nbsp;degrees&nbsp;in&nbsp;preparation&nbsp;for&nbsp;teaching&nbsp;at&nbsp;the&nbsp;college&nbsp;level.&nbsp;The&nbsp;curriculum&nbsp;is&nbsp;designed&nbsp;to&nbsp;prepare&nbsp;students&nbsp;to&nbsp;examine&nbsp;the&nbsp;diverse&nbsp;ways&nbsp;in&nbsp;which&nbsp;writing&nbsp;and&nbsp;literature&nbsp;let&nbsp;us&nbsp;see&nbsp;the&nbsp;past,&nbsp;understand&nbsp;advanced&nbsp;rhetorical&nbsp;and&nbsp;linguistic&nbsp;techniques,&nbsp;and&nbsp;make&nbsp;sense&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;world&nbsp;through&nbsp;narrative.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "0c836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Transfer Success Pathway major eligible",
      "contentHtml": "<p><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/transfer-success-pathway.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Success Pathway</a> major eligible </p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "b8a730af-af06-4545-b0d0-019d68d6b5af",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "The information provided here is subject to change without notice. Please be advised that articulation agreements published here may be updated or added at any time. Be sure to check with a counselor or adviser for the most current requirements. For additional transfer information: For C-ID information: https://c-idsystem.org/courses/ For Common Course Numbering: https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/",
      "contentHtml": "<p></p><p></p><p><strong><em>The&nbsp;information&nbsp;provided&nbsp;here&nbsp;is&nbsp;subject&nbsp;to&nbsp;change&nbsp;without&nbsp;notice.&nbsp;Please&nbsp;be&nbsp;advised&nbsp;that&nbsp;articulation&nbsp;agreements&nbsp;published&nbsp;here&nbsp;may&nbsp;be&nbsp;updated&nbsp;or&nbsp;added&nbsp;at&nbsp;any&nbsp;time.&nbsp;Be&nbsp;sure&nbsp;to&nbsp;check&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;counselor&nbsp;or&nbsp;adviser&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;current&nbsp;requirements.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p></p><p></p><p><strong>For&nbsp;additional&nbsp;transfer&nbsp;information:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>For&nbsp;C-ID&nbsp;information:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://c-idsystem.org/courses/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://c-idsystem.org/courses/</a></li><li>For&nbsp;Common&nbsp;Course&nbsp;Numbering:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/common-course-numbering/</a></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "0a836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 6,
      "content": "(120 UNITS) In addition to the requirements for the major, students must meet all other university requirements for a bachelor’s degree. Please consult the Graduation Requirements for the Bachelor’s Degree section in this catalog for complete information. All courses in the major require a “C” (2.0) or better. When selecting courses — 30 units of which must be upper-division — students are urged to consult a faculty adviser in the Department of English, Comparative Literature and Linguistics. ENGL 101, a graduation requirement for all students, is not part of the English major but is a prerequisite to further work in English. Early Literature Requirement Of the 42 units required for the major, 3 units (beyond those satisfying the Medieval, Early Modern and 18th-Centrury Literature requirement) must focus on Early Literature. This requirement can be satisfied by completing ENGL 211, ENGL 221, CPLT 324, ENGL 416 or a second course in Medieval, Early Modern and 18th-Century Literature.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>(120&nbsp;UNITS)</strong></p><p></p><p>In&nbsp;addition&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;major,&nbsp;students&nbsp;must&nbsp;meet&nbsp;all&nbsp;other&nbsp;university&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;bachelor’s&nbsp;degree.&nbsp;Please&nbsp;consult&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/content.php?catoid=101&amp;navoid=15099\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Graduation&nbsp;Requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;Bachelor’s&nbsp;Degree</a>&nbsp;section&nbsp;in&nbsp;this&nbsp;catalog&nbsp;for&nbsp;complete&nbsp;information.&nbsp;All&nbsp;courses&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;major&nbsp;require&nbsp;a&nbsp;“C”&nbsp;(2.0)&nbsp;or&nbsp;better.</p><p></p><p>When&nbsp;selecting&nbsp;courses&nbsp;—&nbsp;30&nbsp;units&nbsp;of&nbsp;which&nbsp;must&nbsp;be&nbsp;upper-division&nbsp;—&nbsp;students&nbsp;are&nbsp;urged&nbsp;to&nbsp;consult&nbsp;a&nbsp;faculty&nbsp;adviser&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;English,&nbsp;Comparative&nbsp;Literature&nbsp;and&nbsp;Linguistics.&nbsp;ENGL&nbsp;101,&nbsp;a&nbsp;graduation&nbsp;requirement&nbsp;for&nbsp;all&nbsp;students,&nbsp;is&nbsp;not&nbsp;part&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;English&nbsp;major&nbsp;but&nbsp;is&nbsp;a&nbsp;prerequisite&nbsp;to&nbsp;further&nbsp;work&nbsp;in&nbsp;English.</p><p></p><p><strong>Early&nbsp;Literature&nbsp;Requirement</strong></p><p>Of&nbsp;the&nbsp;42&nbsp;units&nbsp;required&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;major,&nbsp;3&nbsp;units&nbsp;(beyond&nbsp;those&nbsp;satisfying&nbsp;the&nbsp;Medieval,&nbsp;Early&nbsp;Modern&nbsp;and&nbsp;18th-Centrury&nbsp;Literature&nbsp;requirement)&nbsp;must&nbsp;focus&nbsp;on&nbsp;Early&nbsp;Literature.&nbsp;This&nbsp;requirement&nbsp;can&nbsp;be&nbsp;satisfied&nbsp;by&nbsp;completing&nbsp;ENGL&nbsp;211,&nbsp;ENGL&nbsp;221,&nbsp;CPLT&nbsp;324,&nbsp;ENGL&nbsp;416&nbsp;or&nbsp;a&nbsp;second&nbsp;course&nbsp;in&nbsp;Medieval,&nbsp;Early&nbsp;Modern&nbsp;and&nbsp;18th-Century&nbsp;Literature.</p>"
    }
  ],
